WEBVTT

00:01.730 --> 00:04.809
Good afternoon and welcome to this

00:04.809 --> 00:06.976
afternoon's cybersecurity Subcommittee

00:06.976 --> 00:09.729
hearing on enterprise security and

00:09.729 --> 00:12.250
information technology operations of

00:12.250 --> 00:14.194
Department of Defense Networks and

00:14.194 --> 00:16.306
Systems . I want to begin by thanking

00:16.306 --> 00:18.194
our witnesses for appearing today

00:18.194 --> 00:19.972
before this subcommittee . Your

00:19.972 --> 00:21.917
testimony arrives at an inflection

00:21.917 --> 00:24.139
point for how the Department of Defense

00:24.139 --> 00:26.799
fights , decides , and wins . This

00:26.799 --> 00:28.743
hearing is fundamentally about war

00:28.743 --> 00:30.910
fighting . The digital backbone of the

00:30.910 --> 00:32.966
Department of Defense is no longer a

00:32.966 --> 00:34.910
support function . It is a weapons

00:34.910 --> 00:37.840
system . Our tanks , ships , aircraft ,

00:38.200 --> 00:40.630
and ground forces depend on connected ,

00:40.880 --> 00:43.319
resilient , and secure networks to

00:43.319 --> 00:45.263
operate at the speed and precision

00:45.263 --> 00:48.040
across vast distances . Sensors all

00:48.040 --> 00:50.430
over the world will connect to shooters

00:50.430 --> 00:53.360
across the theater in a vast kill web .

00:53.650 --> 00:55.889
That must operate faster and more

00:55.889 --> 00:58.669
efficiently than our enemy's systems .

00:59.090 --> 01:01.034
This is especially true for future

01:01.034 --> 01:03.409
conflicts as we continue fielding

01:03.409 --> 01:06.449
software intensive systems designed for

01:06.449 --> 01:08.727
decision advantage and speed of action .

01:10.080 --> 01:13.110
While quantity may have a quality all

01:13.110 --> 01:16.080
of its own , the ability to optimize

01:16.080 --> 01:19.050
our targeting and orient , decide and

01:19.050 --> 01:21.599
act more quickly than the enemy will

01:21.599 --> 01:24.400
likely decide the outcome of the next

01:24.400 --> 01:27.199
major war . The department's cultural

01:27.199 --> 01:30.709
shifts towards recognizing networks and

01:30.709 --> 01:32.820
information technology infrastructure

01:32.820 --> 01:36.459
as a war fighting platform . is one I

01:36.459 --> 01:38.870
agree with . Yet I realize there is

01:38.870 --> 01:42.230
still a long way to go . Software can

01:42.230 --> 01:44.397
be developed and deployed in minutes ,

01:44.397 --> 01:47.040
hours , or days . The bureaucratic

01:47.040 --> 01:49.096
processes governing how we acquire ,

01:49.096 --> 01:51.207
certify , and field it does not match

01:51.207 --> 01:54.279
that timeline . At least not yet . This

01:54.279 --> 01:56.110
reality is no longer merely an

01:56.110 --> 01:58.040
inconvenience . It is a strategic

01:58.040 --> 02:00.940
liability . We have talked long enough

02:00.940 --> 02:02.959
about solving these problems . This

02:02.959 --> 02:06.459
subcommittee wants to see them resolved .

02:07.040 --> 02:09.429
Compounding the urgency is the

02:09.429 --> 02:11.707
condition of the infrastructure itself .

02:11.707 --> 02:13.596
Defense to information technology

02:13.596 --> 02:15.651
budgets have long served as the bill

02:15.651 --> 02:18.440
payer , absorbing cuts to fund near

02:18.440 --> 02:21.389
term priorities . The result is a

02:21.389 --> 02:23.333
technical debt problem of historic

02:23.333 --> 02:26.089
proportions in both hardware and

02:26.089 --> 02:29.130
software . Our adversaries are not

02:29.130 --> 02:31.929
blind to this . Not surprisingly , they

02:31.929 --> 02:34.096
are taking advantage of this blunder .

02:34.759 --> 02:36.981
Every day we delay modernizing is a day

02:36.981 --> 02:39.130
we strengthen their hand in the cyber

02:39.130 --> 02:42.759
domain . As we modernize , speed

02:42.759 --> 02:45.440
without security is not an improvement .

02:45.759 --> 02:47.759
We must be disciplined about not

02:47.759 --> 02:50.309
punting today's problems to the future .

02:50.789 --> 02:53.720
That means patching what we have while

02:53.720 --> 02:56.169
building with foundational security

02:56.440 --> 02:59.990
baked in . This cannot be a

02:59.990 --> 03:03.029
government-only endeavor . The private

03:03.029 --> 03:05.270
sector can move with speed and provide

03:05.270 --> 03:07.214
capabilities the department cannot

03:07.214 --> 03:10.070
match , but partnership only works when

03:10.070 --> 03:12.869
our processes and requirements are

03:12.869 --> 03:16.630
transparent and consistent . We owe

03:16.630 --> 03:19.509
our industry partners clarity , and we

03:19.509 --> 03:22.369
owe our war fighters results .

03:23.339 --> 03:26.020
We must ask what kind of compute

03:26.020 --> 03:28.539
capacity , network resiliency and data

03:28.539 --> 03:31.460
infrastructure our warfighters require ,

03:31.820 --> 03:33.940
not just today , but as artificial

03:33.940 --> 03:35.940
intelligence is deployed at a scale

03:35.940 --> 03:38.419
across the force . If we cannot answer

03:38.419 --> 03:41.339
that question with specificity , we

03:41.339 --> 03:44.100
cannot build toward it . Today the

03:44.100 --> 03:46.211
subcommittee looks forward to hearing

03:46.211 --> 03:47.878
from both of you on where the

03:47.878 --> 03:49.989
department stands in addressing these

03:49.989 --> 03:51.989
efforts . We want to understand how

03:51.989 --> 03:53.767
bureaucratic barriers are being

03:53.767 --> 03:55.822
dismantled and how our processes are

03:55.822 --> 03:57.933
being made more welcoming to industry

03:57.933 --> 04:00.139
partners . It is especially important

04:00.139 --> 04:02.339
for us to hear whether our networks

04:02.339 --> 04:05.179
have the capacity , resilience , and

04:05.179 --> 04:07.419
performance our military requires for

04:07.419 --> 04:10.100
modern warfare against a capable

04:10.100 --> 04:13.809
adversary . Thank you again , and now I

04:13.809 --> 04:15.809
would like to recognize the ranking

04:15.809 --> 04:19.049
member for her remarks . Senator Rosen .

04:20.039 --> 04:22.372
Well , thank you , Chairman Rounds . Uh ,

04:22.372 --> 04:24.150
Ms . Davies , General Stanton ,

04:24.150 --> 04:26.150
appreciate you being here . I wanna

04:26.150 --> 04:27.928
welcome you . And Ms . Davies ,

04:27.928 --> 04:29.650
congratulations on your recent

04:29.650 --> 04:31.872
confirmation and assumption of duties .

04:31.919 --> 04:33.808
And so , Ms . Davies , as you get

04:33.808 --> 04:35.975
settled into this position , we'd like

04:35.975 --> 04:38.308
to hear more about your priorities , uh ,

04:38.308 --> 04:40.419
get some of the ideas of where you're

04:40.419 --> 04:42.475
gonna be placing emphasis on funding

04:42.475 --> 04:44.363
from FY 26 appropriations and any

04:44.363 --> 04:46.363
Reconciliation funding you may have

04:46.363 --> 04:48.252
received as well . And so without

04:48.252 --> 04:50.475
discussing specifics , it would also be

04:50.475 --> 04:52.419
helpful to know where we might see

04:52.419 --> 04:54.697
significant budget swings for programs ,

04:54.697 --> 04:56.808
so we're not surprised when the FY 27

04:56.808 --> 04:59.086
president's budget request is released .

04:59.369 --> 05:01.313
That request is already nearly two

05:01.313 --> 05:03.425
months late . It's not expected for a

05:03.425 --> 05:05.647
few more weeks , and that leaves little

05:05.647 --> 05:07.813
time in our NDAA process to delve into

05:07.813 --> 05:09.980
the details , and it's critical for us

05:09.980 --> 05:12.313
to be able to do that . General Stanton ,

05:12.313 --> 05:14.369
I wanna welcome you back . Thank you

05:14.369 --> 05:16.536
for your years of service . I hope you

05:16.536 --> 05:18.758
will also share your thoughts on all of

05:18.758 --> 05:20.758
these topics as they relate to your

05:20.758 --> 05:22.591
role as Director for the Defense

05:22.591 --> 05:24.313
Information Systems Agency and

05:24.313 --> 05:26.647
commander for the Department of Defense ,

05:26.647 --> 05:29.070
Cyber Defense Command . As the

05:29.070 --> 05:31.181
organization charged with running DOD

05:31.181 --> 05:32.792
networks , you have a unique

05:32.792 --> 05:34.903
operational perspective on how policy

05:34.903 --> 05:37.014
decisions from the department CIO are

05:37.014 --> 05:39.014
translated well , into action . But

05:39.014 --> 05:40.792
that also means that you have a

05:40.792 --> 05:42.681
slightly different view as to the

05:42.681 --> 05:44.737
resourcing and workforce needs . The

05:44.737 --> 05:46.792
implementation of technology for the

05:46.792 --> 05:49.014
warfighters is different maybe than the

05:49.014 --> 05:51.237
development , right ? And the impact of

05:51.237 --> 05:53.292
technical debt on the ability of our

05:53.292 --> 05:55.514
department to modernize . You can speak

05:55.514 --> 05:57.737
